Why each element is added:

Second Load Balancer (HAproxy cluster):
Added to avoid single point of failure.
If one load balancer fails, the other continues handling traffic.

Web Server (separate):
Handles static content (HTML, CSS, JS).
Improves performance and reduces load on application server.

Application Server (separate):
Handles business logic and dynamic requests.
Keeps logic separated from web server.

Database Server (separate):
Stores data independently.
Improves scalability and performance.

Extra Server:
Used to host separated components.
Allows better scaling and resource management.


Key concept:

Web Server vs Application Server:

Web Server (Nginx):
- Handles HTTP requests
- Serves static files
- Forwards dynamic requests

Application Server:
- Executes application code
- Handles business logic
- Communicates with database
